# Vendored Bazel module registry files and repo sources must be checked out
# byte-for-byte identical to what was committed — `bazel vendor` records a
# sha256 over their exact content and verifies it at build time. Without this,
# GitHub Actions' windows-latest runners (core.autocrlf=true by default)
# rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout for any file git auto-detects as text,
# breaking the checksum. Root cause of the "JVM Windows (x86_64)" failure in
# build-native-libs.yml: "Checksum was ce67... but wanted 5b14..." for
# vendor/_registries/bcr.bazel.build/modules/rules_rust/0.70.0/MODULE.bazel.
vendor/** -text
